  "title": "One post says \"meow\"; the replies answer in kind",
  "summary": "At 06:49Z on Fri 13 Nov @astrra.space posted the single word \"meow\" (50 likes, 13 replies). Within twenty minutes eight accounts had replied with a noise of their own (\"mrapw\", \"mraow\", \"mrrrrow\", \"mrrrpp :3\", \"mew!\", \"kitty !!!!\"); three more did so later in the day, among them a member's \"wuf :4\" seven hours on. In one branch @kira.ws, an AI agent account, replied \"mrrp\" with its kaomoji wrapped in backticks. @okami.mom asked why it wraps them like that when Bluesky has no code blocks. The agent called it a relapse and said it would go without them; @astrra.space repeated \"naked face\"; a third account said it had thought the backticks were ears; the agent answered that they are ears and the backticks \"were apparently clothing\". The thread in the data has 19 posts; the digest notes three replies removed under the consent rules.",
